From 1fff11e370d6b7a764f3e7926361584115067359 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sasha Levin <sashal@kernel.org>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 20:13:01 -0500
Subject: ext4: don't track metadata buffers on an inode during fast commit
 replay

From: Theodore Ts'o <tytso@mit.edu>

[ Upstream commit aceadbccd428fb8e6593b27a3091d961f80225d1 ]

Fast commit replay runs without a journal handle and before
EXT4_SB(sb)->s_journal is set, so it effectively runs in nojournal mode.
__ext4_handle_dirty_metadata() then hands every extent tree block and
directory block it dirties to mmb_mark_buffer_dirty().

Commit d4fdde3257a5 ("fs: set I_METADATA_WRITEBACK in
mmb_mark_buffer_dirty()") sets this flag on the inode, which can
trigger a NULL pointer dereference on a per-cpu pointer during the
fast commit replay.  This is because the iput at the end of each fast
commit update triggers write_inode_now(), and with
I_METADATA_WRITEBACK set, writeback_single_inode() will end up calling
ext4_writepages(), before ext4_percpu_param_init() has initialized
s_writepages_rwsem.

A similar crash was fixed in commit 0ecd56573c1f ("ext4: Avoid
entering writeback paths during fastcommit replay") by not setting
this flag in ext4_mark_iloc_dirty().  This commit applies the same fix
to __ext4_handle_dirty_metadata().

Once the fast commit replay is complete, jbd2_journal_recover() syncs
and flushes the whole block device, o the buffer is still written out
before the mount proceeds.

Reproduced with generic/311 using "-O inline_data,fast_commit" (the
ext4/adv test configuration).

Fixes: d4fdde3257a5 ("fs: set I_METADATA_WRITEBACK in mmb_mark_buffer_dirty()")
Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org
Signed-off-by: Theodore Ts'o <tytso@mit.edu>
Signed-off-by: Sasha Levin <sashal@kernel.org>
---
 fs/ext4/ext4_jbd2.c | 14 +++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/fs/ext4/ext4_jbd2.c b/fs/ext4/ext4_jbd2.c
index 53ddedb52a6f7..d81ce9b8a5407 100644
--- a/fs/ext4/ext4_jbd2.c
+++ b/fs/ext4/ext4_jbd2.c
@@ -412,7 +412,19 @@ int __ext4_handle_dirty_metadata(const char *where, unsigned int line,
 					 err);
 		}
 	} else {
-		if (inode) {
+		/*
+		 * Fast commit replay runs without a handle, before the
+		 * writeback paths are set up.  Don't track the buffer in the
+		 * inode's metadata list then: mmb_mark_buffer_dirty() sets
+		 * I_METADATA_WRITEBACK, and since the superblock isn't active
+		 * yet the iput() ending the replay step writes the inode out
+		 * and enters ext4_writepages() before s_writepages_rwsem is
+		 * initialized.  Journal recovery flushes the whole block
+		 * device once replay is done, so the buffer still gets
+		 * written.
+		 */
+		if (inode && !(EXT4_SB(inode->i_sb)->s_mount_state &
+			       EXT4_FC_REPLAY)) {
 			if (!ext4_i_metadata_bhs(inode))
 				ext4_inode_attach_mmb(inode);
 			mmb_mark_buffer_dirty(bh, ext4_i_metadata_bhs(inode));
